- op: update  # 2a16
  at: '2026-05-19T21:26:18Z'  # 2a16
  by: agent  # 2a16
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 2a16
  clock: 4  # 2a16
  nonce: 2a16  # 2a16
  set:  # 2a16
    title: "cli.py _NOISE_KINDS overloads kind='table' — drops SQL CREATE TABLE entities alongside TOML config tables"  # 2a16
    description: "**Found via self-analysis dogfooding on 2026-05-17 (round 17); diagnosis revised 2026-05-19 after empirical investigation.**\n\n**Original hypothesis (incorrect; preserved for context).** The schema 0.2.2 → 0.8.0 migration left 4 framework linkers (event-sourcing, http, graphql-resolver, database-query) targeting deleted kind names in their edge-construction code.\n\n**Actual root cause.** A single CLI-level noise filter overloads `kind=\"table\"`:\n\n- `cli.py:7370-7381` `_NOISE_KINDS` includes `\"table\"`, intended to suppress TOML `[section]` table headers (config noise).\n- `cli.py:7390-7403` `_is_noise(sym)` checks only `sym.kind`, ignoring `sym.language`.\n- SQL analyzer (`sql.py:225`) emits `kind=\"table\"` for `CREATE TABLE` constructs (schema entities, NOT noise).\n- The filter drops both kinds, collapsing all `kind=\"table\"` to 0 in final output.\n\n**Empirical verification.**\n\nAfter `run_all_analyzers()` returns: 59 total `kind=\"table\"` symbols — 1 from `sql-v1` (the `users` table from `tests/fixtures/schema-coverage-corpus/sql/schema.sql`) and 58 from `toml-v1` (TOML [section] headers across pyproject.toml files).\n\nAfter `cli.py:_is_noise` filter (default `include_docs=False`): 0 `kind=\"table\"` symbols. All TOML tables intentionally dropped; the 1 SQL table dropped accidentally.\n\nDownstream symptom for the database_query linker: `ctx.symbols` contains 0 `kind=\"table\"` symbols, so `_get_table_symbols()` returns `[]`, `table_lookup` is empty, and the 34 detected db_query call_sites can never link to a table.\n\n**The other 3 linkers' 0-edge results are unrelated to this bug** and turn out to be expected given the current codebase content:\n\n| Linker | 0-edge cause |\n|---|---|\n| event_sourcing | 3 publishers (events: back/dispatch/item-select) and 11 subscribers (events: activate/close/fetch/load/...). Zero event-name overlap. Linker correctly emits 0 edges. |\n| http | 18 client calls to /api/users, /api/orders, /api/products. 8 server routes to /api/items, /health, /ws. Fixtures live in different test directories with no URL-pattern overlap. |\n| graphql_resolver | 11 graphql_resolver symbols emitted. Zero GraphQL schema files (`.graphql`/`.gql`) in repo. No upstream type/field symbols to link to. |\n\nUnit tests verify each linker emits edges given matching synthetic input (`assert len(result.edges) == 1` etc. in `test_*_linker.py`; 338 passing tests across the 4 broken-linker test files). Linker edge-construction code is migrated correctly to the new framework_role / call_kind / language schema.\n\n**Fix.**\n\nAdd a language guard to `cli.py:_is_noise` mirroring the existing CSS-variable carve-out:\n\n```python\n_CONFIG_LANGUAGES = frozenset({\"toml\", \"ini\", \"properties\"})\n\ndef _is_noise(sym: \"Symbol\") -> bool:\n    if sym.kind in _NOISE_KINDS:\n        return True\n    if sym.kind == \"variable\" and sym.language in _CSS_LANGUAGES:\n        return True\n    if sym.kind == \"table\" and sym.language in _CONFIG_LANGUAGES:\n        return True\n    ...\n```\n\nAnd remove `\"table\"` from `_NOISE_KINDS`.\n\n**Bakeoff target.** Any repo with SQL DDL files + database query call sites in code. The schema-coverage-corpus fixture in hypergumbo itself is the minimal reproducer (1 SQL `users` table, 34 DB query call_sites in test/lab files referencing `users`/`items`/`orders`/etc.).\n\n**Cross-references.**\n- `INV-rovuj` precedent: language guard pattern for cross-language kind overlap (C++ vs Python `Init` method disambiguation).\n- `audit-findings 0006/0007` (Cluster A) noted `property`, `label`, `heading`, `paragraph` as AXIS_LANGUAGE_CONSTRUCT — semantics differ per language. `table` belongs to the same axis but was not audited explicitly.\n- Conceptual-leak candidate per the Fundamental Concept Audit playbook: `kind=\"table\"` fails the Apex/Peer-overloading test (TOML table-as-config-section vs SQL table-as-schema-entity).\n\n**Notebook reference.** `~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/notebookjournal_05162026_0438.md` Round 17 section (original 0-edge observation); 2026-05-19 follow-up investigation pinpointed the noise-filter root cause."  # 2a16
    fields:  # 2a16
      statement: "The kind=\"table\" symbol value must distinguish SQL CREATE TABLE entities (first-class, must reach final output) from TOML/INI [section] table headers (config noise, filtered by default). Currently cli.py:7370-7381 _NOISE_KINDS treats all kind=\"table\" as documentation noise, dropping 1 valid sql-v1 table Symbol from hypergumbo self-analysis on every run. Downstream effect: database_query linker has 34 db_query call_sites but 0 edges because the upstream kind=\"table\" nodes never reach ctx.symbols."  # 2a16
      root_cause: "cli.py:_NOISE_KINDS frozenset includes \"table\", added when the only producer was the TOML/INI config-table emitter. The SQL analyzer (sql.py:225) emits the same kind=\"table\" literal for CREATE TABLE constructs — entirely different concept. The filter at cli.py:7390-7403 _is_noise(sym) checks only kind, not language. Fix: extend _is_noise to filter kind=\"table\" only when sym.language is in a config-language set (toml/ini/properties); SQL tables pass through. Pattern mirrors the existing CSS-variable carve-out at cli.py:7393-7394 (\"variable\" is noise in CSS but real in Python/Go/YAML). Verified: SQL analyzer table is present after run_all_analyzers (1 sql-v1 + 58 toml-v1 kind=table symbols) but absent from final output (0). The other three linkers in the original INV-bovif scope (event_sourcing/http/graphql_resolver) report 0 edges for unrelated reasons (no overlap between codebase pub/sub event names, no overlap between fixture HTTP client URLs and server route paths, no GraphQL schema files in repo) — not linker bugs; verified via 338 passing unit tests with synthetic overlapping fixtures."  # 2a16
